# The ruling: if Leonardo is dealt lethal damage at the same time that you gain life, he won't receive a counter from his
# last ability in time to save him. Leonardo (1/1, lifelink) attacks on turn 5 and Bot2's Llanowar Elves (1/1) blocks: the
# combat damage is dealt at once (CR 510.2), Bot1 gains 1 from his lifelink, and he dies to the Elves' 1 as a state-based
# action (CR 704.5g) before his trigger is put on the stack (CR 704.3, 117.5); it resolves with him gone (CR 400.7) and puts
# no counter on anything. Had the counter come first he would be a 2/2 with 1 damage, alive. The Elves die to his 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Leonardo, Cutting Edge
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Leonardo, Cutting Edge)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Leonardo, Cutting Edge
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
